---
import type { CollectionEntry } from 'astro:content';

interface Props {
  issue: CollectionEntry<'issues'>;
}

const { issue } = Astro.props;

const issueNumber = String(issue.data.issueNumber).padStart(3, '0');
const publishDate = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', {
  month: 'long',
  day: 'numeric',
  year: 'numeric',
}).format(issue.data.publishDate);
---

<article class="friend-issue">
  <header class="issue-masthead">
    <div class="issue-masthead-title">Issue No. {issueNumber}</div>
    <div class="masthead-line"></div>
    <div class="issue-meta">
      <span>{issue.data.label}</span>
      <span>{publishDate}</span>
      <span>{issue.data.readTime}</span>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="spread hero-spread" aria-labelledby="friend-title">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="section-label">A Study In Nearness</p>
      <h1 id="friend-title">The Friend<br /><em>Jesus</em></h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">{issue.data.description}</p>
      <div class="hero-quote">
        <span>John 15:15</span>
        <p>When you received the gospel, you received a Lord, a Savior, and a great friend.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <figure class="room-scene">
      <img
        src="/the-friend-jesus-hero.jpg"
        alt="An open Bible on a wooden desk under warm lamp light."
        loading="eager"
        decoding="async"
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
      <figcaption>Attention is not the same thing as friendship.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="spread ache-spread">
    <div class="spread-number">01</div>
    <div class="copy-column">
      <p class="section-label">The Ache</p>
      <h2>You can have attention and still not have friendship.</h2>
      <div class="body-copy">
        <p>
          You can be in every group chat and still feel unknown. You can laugh with people all day and still go home
          feeling like nobody really knows you. A lot of us struggle to name that honestly. We call it tiredness, or
          stress, or one of those seasons.
        </p>
        <p>But sometimes the problem is simpler than that. Sometimes you are lonely.</p>
        <p>
          Loneliness changes how you think and what you settle for. Noise can start to feel like love. Proximity can
          start to feel like closeness. Being around people can start to feel like being known.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="margin-note">
      <span>Reader's Margin</span>
      <p>Noise can imitate nearness for a while. It cannot replace being known.</p>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="spread personal-spread">
    <div class="spread-number">02</div>
    <div class="personal-rule"></div>
    <div class="personal-copy">
      <p class="section-label">Not From A Distance</p>
      <p>
        I am not saying that from a distance. I have lived with loneliness for a long time, and even as I write this, I
        still feel it sometimes. I am fresh out of a dating relationship. I was laid off from my job. There are other
        things in my life right now that I would not have chosen.
      </p>
      <p>So this is not just an idea to me. I am writing from pain, but also from discovery.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="discovery-line">This is why the words of Jesus matter.</div>
  </section>

  <section class="spread thesis-spread">
    <p class="section-label">The Claim</p>
    <h2>Jesus calls his people friends.</h2>
    <div class="thesis-grid">
      <p>
        Many believers know him as Lord, Savior, and King. All of that is true. Many still struggle to live with another
        truth.
      </p>
      <p>
        That line can sound soft if we rush it. It can turn into church language with no weight in real life. So we need
        to say the point carefully.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="large-line">When you received the gospel, you received a Lord, a Savior, and a great friend.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="spread garden-spread">
    <div class="spread-number">03</div>
    <div class="garden-texture" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="copy-column">
      <p class="section-label">The Beginning</p>
      <h2>God began with nearness.</h2>
      <div class="body-copy">
        <p>Sometimes we talk as if God started far away and later decided to come close. The Bible tells us something different.</p>
        <p>Nearness was there from the beginning.</p>
        <p>
          Genesis 2 shows us a God who made man with care and placed him in a garden with purpose. This was life with
          God. It was fellowship, instruction, presence, and trust.
        </p>
        <p>
          Then sin entered the world, and shame followed it quickly. When Adam and Eve hid, it showed that sin produces
          guilt and distance.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <blockquote class="scripture-block">
      <span>Genesis 3:8-9</span>
      <p>
        "And they heard the sound of the Lord God walking in the garden in the cool of the day, and the man and his wife
        hid themselves from the presence of the Lord God among the trees of the garden. But the Lord God called to the
        man and said to him, 'Where are you?'"
      </p>
    </blockquote>
    <p class="after-fall">After the fall, God called first.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="spread history-spread">
    <div class="spread-number">04</div>
    <p class="section-label">Across Scripture</p>
    <h2>God kept moving toward people.</h2>
    <div class="history-rail">
      <div>
        <span>Hebrews 1:1-2</span>
        <p>God spoke in many times and many ways, and in these last days he has spoken to us by his Son.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span>Exodus 33:11</span>
        <p>"Thus the Lord used to speak to Moses face to face, as a man speaks to his friend."</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span>James 2:23</span>
        <p>"Abraham believed God, and it was counted to him as righteousness" and he was called a friend of God.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span>Jeremiah 9:24</span>
        <p>"But let him who boasts boast in this, that he understands and knows me."</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="history-close">
      God was inviting people into more than obedience. He was inviting them to know him. Friendship with God has a
      history. It has roots. We see it across Scripture.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="spread john-spread">
    <div class="spread-number">05</div>
    <div class="john-header">
      <p class="section-label">The Center</p>
      <h2>Jesus says it plainly.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="john-copy">
      <p>Then the life of Jesus makes it plain.</p>
      <p>
        John 1:14 says, "And the Word became flesh and dwelt among us, and we have seen his glory, glory as of the only
        Son from the Father, full of grace and truth."
      </p>
      <p>God came near in a person.</p>
    </div>
    <blockquote class="john-verse">
      <span>John 15:12-15</span>
      <p>
        "This is my commandment, that you love one another as I have loved you. Greater love has no one than this, that
        someone lay down his life for his friends. You are my friends if you do what I command you. No longer do I call
        you servants, for the servant does not know what his master is doing but I have called you friends, for all that
        I have heard from my Father I have made known to you."
      </p>
    </blockquote>
    <p class="john-bottom">Jesus chose that word with care. He calls them friends.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="spread lord-spread">
    <div class="spread-number">06</div>
    <div class="copy-column">
      <p class="section-label">The Reverence</p>
      <h2>Friend, but still Lord.</h2>
      <div class="body-copy">
        <p>Jesus is still Lord.</p>
        <p>
          This is where people can go wrong. If you hear that Jesus calls you friend, you can start shrinking him in your
          mind. You start treating him casually. You lose reverence.
        </p>
        <p>Friendship with Jesus is intimate and reverent.</p>
        <p>
          He draws near without becoming less than he is. He speaks openly, but he still commands. He loves warmly, but
          he is still the Son of God. His friendship is real, and he remains above us.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="reverence-stamp">He draws near without becoming small.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="spread cross-spread">
    <div class="spread-number">07</div>
    <p class="section-label">The Proof</p>
    <h2>The cross proves what kind of friend he is.</h2>
    <div class="cross-layout">
      <blockquote>
        <span>John 15:13</span>
        <p>"Greater love has no one than this, that someone lay down his life for his friends."</p>
      </blockquote>
      <div class="cross-mark" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="cross-copy">
        <p>Friendship becomes sentimental when we leave it undefined.</p>
        <p>Jesus tied friendship to sacrifice.</p>
        <p>This is what makes Jesus the greatest friend. His friendship led him to the cross.</p>
        <p>
          Jesus' friendship rises above every human example. Ordinary loyalty falls short beside a friend who gives his
          life for you.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="calvary-line">The cross is the proof. If you want to know what kind of friend Jesus is, start at Calvary.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="spread practice-spread">
    <div class="spread-number">08</div>
    <p class="section-label">The Shape Of Love</p>
    <h2>His friendship should shape how believers love people.</h2>
    <div class="practice-grid">
      <p>If Jesus befriends people this way, then Christians should stop treating people like projects, props, or categories.</p>
      <p>That means genuine care. It means noticing people, making room for them, and treating them with steady kindness.</p>
      <p>So love people well. Do good without demanding a return. Care for people without turning them into opportunities.</p>
      <p>It means loving people enough to tell the truth without joining them in sin.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="practice-verses">
      <blockquote>
        <span>John 13:35</span>
        <p>"By this all people will know that you are my disciples, if you have love for one another."</p>
      </blockquote>
      <blockquote>
        <span>Romans 12:15</span>
        <p>"Rejoice with those who rejoice, weep with those who weep."</p>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="spread faith-spread">
    <div class="spread-number">09</div>
    <div class="copy-column">
      <p class="section-label">The Door</p>
      <h2>Friendship with God comes by faith.</h2>
      <div class="body-copy">
        <p>How does a person become a friend of God?</p>
        <p>
          A person becomes a friend of God by faith. Impressiveness, cleaning yourself up first, and spiritual performance
          are the wrong place to look.
        </p>
        <p>
          James 2:23 takes us back to Abraham: "Abraham believed God, and it was counted to him as righteousness" and he
          was called a friend of God.
        </p>
        <p>Friendship with God is received by trusting him.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="faith-note">
      <span>Good News</span>
      <p>Jesus bore sin and grief and sorrow so that sinners could be brought near.</p>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="spread close-spread">
    <p class="section-label">The Nearness</p>
    <h2>He brings his people near.</h2>
    <div class="close-copy">
      <p>Some people have attention and still need true friendship.</p>
      <p>Some believers know Jesus is powerful. They struggle to believe he is near.</p>
      <p>The gospel answer to loneliness is this: the Son of God came near, spoke plainly, laid down his life, and now calls his people friends.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="final-line">He brings his people near.</p>
    <div class="colophon">The Friend Jesus · Nevertheless Press · {publishDate}</div>
  </section>
</article>

<style>
  :root {
    --friend-cream: #f7f0e2;
    --friend-paper: #efe2c9;
    --friend-ink: #12110d;
    --friend-green: #143d33;
    --friend-green-deep: #0d2923;
    --friend-gold: #c79d3f;
    --friend-clay: #9c4f2f;
    --friend-olive: #61713d;
    --friend-shadow: rgba(18, 17, 13, 0.18);
  }

  .friend-issue {
    background: var(--friend-cream);
    color: var(--friend-ink);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .issue-masthead {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    padding: 1.2rem clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    background: var(--friend-ink);
    color: var(--friend-cream);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(199, 157, 63, 0.28);
  }

  .issue-masthead-title {
    font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.28em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--friend-gold);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .masthead-line {
    height: 1px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(199, 157, 63, 0.8), transparent);
  }

  .issue-meta,
  .section-label,
  .hero-quote span,
  .room-scene figcaption,
  .margin-note span,
  .scripture-block span,
  .history-rail span,
  .john-verse span,
  .cross-layout span,
  .practice-verses span,
  .faith-note span,
  .colophon {
    font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .issue-meta {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    font-size: 0.58rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    color: rgba(247, 240, 226, 0.58);
  }

  .spread {
    min-height: 100vh;
    position: relative;
    padding: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 8rem) clamp(1.5rem, 7vw, 7rem);
  }

  .section-label {
    margin: 0 0 1.2rem;
    color: var(--friend-clay);
    font-size: 0.64rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.32em;
  }

  h1,
  h2,
  .large-line,
  .discovery-line,
  .after-fall,
  .john-bottom,
  .reverence-stamp,
  .calvary-line,
  .final-line,
  .spread-number {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
  }

  h1,
  h2,
  p,
  blockquote {
    margin: 0;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(4.8rem, 14vw, 13rem);
    line-height: 0.82;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    max-width: 7ch;
  }

  h1 em {
    color: var(--friend-gold);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 8.5vw, 8rem);
    line-height: 0.92;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    max-width: 11ch;
  }

  .body-copy {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    max-width: 62ch;
    font-size: clamp(1.08rem, 1.8vw, 1.32rem);
    line-height: 1.76;
    color: rgba(18, 17, 13, 0.78);
  }

  .body-copy p + p {
    margin-top: 1.2rem;
  }

  .spread-number {
    position: absolute;
    right: clamp(1rem, 5vw, 5rem);
    top: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 5rem);
    font-size: clamp(6rem, 18vw, 18rem);
    line-height: 0.8;
    font-weight: 900;
    color: rgba(18, 17, 13, 0.05);
    pointer-events: none;
    user-select: none;
  }

  .hero-spread {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.82fr) minmax(360px, 0.9fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 6rem);
    align-items: center;
    background:
      linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(247, 240, 226, 0.96), rgba(239, 226, 201, 0.78)),
      radial-gradient(circle at 70% 20%, rgba(199, 157, 63, 0.22), transparent 38%);
  }

  .hero-lede {
    max-width: 35ch;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2vw, 1.5rem);
    line-height: 1.62;
    color: rgba(18, 17, 13, 0.66);
  }

  .hero-quote {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    max-width: 42ch;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--friend-gold);
    padding-left: 1.4rem;
  }

  .hero-quote span {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
    font-size: 0.6rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    color: var(--friend-clay);
  }

  .hero-quote p {
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.5vw, 2rem);
    line-height: 1.28;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .room-scene {
    min-height: clamp(560px, 72vh, 820px);
    margin: 0;
    position: relative;
    isolation: isolate;
    background: var(--friend-ink);
    box-shadow: 0 30px 90px rgba(18, 17, 13, 0.2);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .room-scene::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 1;
    background:
      linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(18, 17, 13, 0.04), rgba(18, 17, 13, 0.46)),
      radial-gradient(circle at 70% 18%, rgba(247, 240, 226, 0.18), transparent 36%);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .room-scene img {
    display: block;
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center;
    filter: saturate(0.9) contrast(1.04);
  }

  .room-scene figcaption {
    position: absolute;
    left: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    bottom: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    z-index: 2;
    max-width: 25ch;
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: rgba(247, 240, 226, 0.72);
  }

  .ache-spread {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(220px, 0.38fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 7vw, 7rem);
    align-items: center;
    background: var(--friend-ink);
    color: var(--friend-cream);
  }

  .ache-spread .body-copy {
    color: rgba(247, 240, 226, 0.78);
  }

  .ache-spread .spread-number {
    color: rgba(247, 240, 226, 0.06);
  }

  .margin-note,
  .faith-note {
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(199, 157, 63, 0.55);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(199, 157, 63, 0.24);
    padding: 1.4rem 0;
  }

  .margin-note span,
  .faith-note span {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--friend-gold);
    font-size: 0.58rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
  }

  .margin-note p,
  .faith-note p {
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.6vw, 2.1rem);
    line-height: 1.35;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .personal-spread {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.18fr minmax(0, 0.86fr) minmax(260px, 0.55fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5rem);
    align-items: center;
    background: var(--friend-green);
    color: var(--friend-cream);
  }

  .personal-spread .spread-number,
  .john-spread .spread-number,
  .cross-spread .spread-number,
  .lord-spread .spread-number {
    color: rgba(247, 240, 226, 0.06);
  }

  .personal-rule {
    width: 1px;
    height: 70vh;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, transparent, var(--friend-gold), transparent);
  }

  .personal-copy {
    max-width: 55ch;
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.4vw, 1.8rem);
    line-height: 1.62;
    color: rgba(247, 240, 226, 0.82);
  }

  .personal-copy p + p {
    margin-top: 1.4rem;
  }

  .discovery-line {
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 5.5rem);
    line-height: 0.98;
    color: var(--friend-gold);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .thesis-spread {
    background: var(--friend-paper);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .thesis-spread h2 {
    max-width: 12ch;
  }

  .thesis-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 34rem));
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 5rem);
    margin-top: 3rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 1.8vw, 1.35rem);
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: rgba(18, 17, 13, 0.7);
  }

  .large-line {
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem);
    max-width: 21ch;
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 6.5rem);
    line-height: 0.98;
    color: var(--friend-green);
  }

  .garden-spread {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.82fr) minmax(300px, 0.72fr);
    gap: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 6rem);
    align-items: center;
    background: #eef1dc;
  }

  .garden-texture {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 18% 28%, rgba(97, 113, 61, 0.28), transparent 25%),
      radial-gradient(circle at 86% 34%, rgba(20, 61, 51, 0.18), transparent 28%),
      linear-gradient(135deg, transparent 0 48%, rgba(97, 113, 61, 0.13) 49% 51%, transparent 52%);
    opacity: 0.65;
  }

  .garden-spread > *:not(.garden-texture) {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .scripture-block,
  .john-verse,
  .cross-layout blockquote,
  .practice-verses blockquote {
    border-left: 4px solid var(--friend-gold);
    padding-left: clamp(1.2rem, 2.6vw, 2rem);
  }

  .scripture-block span,
  .john-verse span,
  .cross-layout span,
  .practice-verses span {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--friend-clay);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
  }

  .scripture-block p {
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.4vw, 2rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .after-fall {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    justify-self: end;
    max-width: 20ch;
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 5.8rem);
    line-height: 0.95;
    color: var(--friend-green);
  }

  .history-spread {
    background: var(--friend-cream);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .history-spread h2 {
    max-width: 12ch;
  }

  .history-rail {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(18, 17, 13, 0.18);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(18, 17, 13, 0.18);
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }

  .history-rail div {
    padding: 2rem 1.4rem;
    border-right: 1px solid rgba(18, 17, 13, 0.14);
  }

  .history-rail div:last-child {
    border-right: 0;
  }

  .history-rail span {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--friend-clay);
    font-size: 0.6rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
  }

  .history-rail p {
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.55vw, 1.18rem);
    line-height: 1.68;
    color: rgba(18, 17, 13, 0.72);
  }

  .history-close {
    max-width: 58ch;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.18rem, 2vw, 1.5rem);
    line-height: 1.68;
    color: var(--friend-green);
  }

  .john-spread {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.58fr) minmax(0, 0.9fr);
    gap: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 6rem);
    align-items: center;
    background: var(--friend-green-deep);
    color: var(--friend-cream);
  }

